      "artist": "P4K1T0",
      "description": "Mosaic mural in Parque de Alfonso Torres of Cartagena (Spain), work of the painter Enrique Gabriel Navarro in 1972.\nIn the mural a woman is seen holding before Carthago Nova the two mural crowns that were awarded by Scipio Africanus for the taking of the city in the Second Punic War, and a fragment of the the Poem of Scipio is quoted in the lower left:\n\n\"It was just, because if to Rome, as a codex tells, every assaulted city cost a crown, Cartagena was a force that cost two!\"",
